From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:25:39 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] DIAG (test build only): FSP-M UPD dump, no HECI retries

Not for the release. Dumps the whole FSPM_UPD before FspMemoryInit (Dasharo's method in dasharo-issues #1874) and sets DisableHeciRetry, to find the constant 15.24 s in FspMemoryInit with a valid training cache and the ME disabled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb | 4 ++++
 src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c    | 5 +++++
 2 files changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
index 9b19d1e419..f4e0236cd3 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/devicetree.cb
@@ -1,6 +1,10 @@
 ## SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 
 chip soc/intel/cannonlake
+	# DIAG (test build only): no retries of FSP-M's HECI messages, with the
+	# ME disabled (the 15 s in FspMemoryInit)
+	register "DisableHeciRetry" = "true"
+
 	# Power limits from the processor's TDP, as the OEM firmware (its PL2
 	# override is on with 0, the processor default): PL1 the TDP, PL2 1.25
 	# times it. A fixed PL2 of 65 W let a 35 W T model draw 65 W for 28 s,
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
index d0ea9454c5..c7316304e0 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/m720q_m920q/romstage.c
@@ -6,6 +6,7 @@
 #include <device/pci_ops.h>
 #include <fsp/api.h>
 #include <mainboard/ec.h>
+#include <lib.h>
 #include <option.h>
 #include <soc/cnl_memcfg_init.h>
 #include <soc/romstage.h>
@@ -126,4 +127,8 @@ void mainboard_memory_init_params(FSPM_UPD *memupd)
 		memupd->FspmConfig.PcieRpEnableMask &= ~(1 << 5);
 
 	memupd->FspmConfig.Peg0Enable = peg_enable(memupd);
+
+	/* DIAG (test build only): every FSP-M parameter, as FSP-M gets it */
+	printk(BIOS_DEBUG, "DIAG FSPM_UPD (%zu bytes):\n", sizeof(*memupd));
+	hexdump(memupd, sizeof(*memupd));
 }
